{{/*
The profile describes privilege level, not employer. `managed` is the MDM-enrolled
work Mac with no admin rights; `owned` is the personal Mac with root.

promptChoiceOnce asks exactly once, at `chezmoi init`, and stores the answer in
~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml. It is never re-derived from the hostname: Macs get
renamed, and a silently switched profile is a failure mode you discover a week later.

The prompt text below is also the lookup key for `--promptChoice`, which is how CI
answers this question without a TTY. That flag takes comma-separated `key=value`
pairs, so a prompt containing a comma or an `=` cannot be matched and the prompt
fires anyway - returning the prompt string itself as the answer, silently. Keep the
text short and free of both characters; the long explanation lives in README.md.
*/ -}}
{{- $profile := promptChoiceOnce . "profile" "Machine profile" (list "managed" "owned") -}}

{{/*
`chezmoi init --source DIR` does not persist DIR anywhere. Without the line below, a
later bare `chezmoi apply` falls back to ~/.local/share/chezmoi, finds nothing there
and silently applies nothing. Record the directory init actually used.
*/ -}}
sourceDir = {{ .chezmoi.sourceDir | quote }}

[data]
    profile = {{ $profile | quote }}
